{"timestamp": "2025-07-29T21:10:19.604635", "function_name": "craft", "function_body": "    def _hash_state(state):\n        \"\"\"\n        Creates a hashable representation of a CraftState.\n        Uses the grid, inventory, position, and direction.\n        \"\"\"\n        # Convert numpy arrays to bytes for efficient hashing\n        # This ensures the state representation is unique and immutable\n        grid_bytes = state.grid.tobytes()\n        inventory_bytes = state.inventory.tobytes()\n        return (grid_bytes, inventory_bytes, state.pos, state.dir)\n\n    # Get the initial state from the environment's current state\n    initial_state = env._current_state\n\n    # Get the integer values for all possible actions from the environment\n    # Sorting ensures a consistent exploration order, though for BFS, it doesn't affect optimality.\n    action_map = env.action_specs()\n    ACTIONS = sorted(action_map.values())\n\n    # Initialize a queue for BFS: each element is (current_state, path_to_current_state)\n    # collections.deque is used for efficient popleft operations\n    queue = collections.deque([(initial_state, [])])\n\n    # Initialize a set to store visited states (using their hashable representations)\n    # This prevents cycles and redundant exploration\n    visited = {_hash_state(initial_state)}\n\n    # Check if the desired item is already present in the initial state's inventory\n    if initial_state.satisfies(None, item):\n        return []  # Goal already met, no actions needed\n\n    # Perform Breadth-First Search\n    while queue:\n        current_state, path = queue.popleft()\n\n        # Explore all possible actions from the current state\n        for action in ACTIONS:\n            # Simulate taking the action to get the next state\n            # CraftState.step returns (reward, new_state)\n            _, next_state = current_state.step(action)\n\n            # Get the hashable representation of the next state\n            next_state_hash = _hash_state(next_state)\n\n            # If this next state has not been visited before\n            if next_state_hash not in visited:\n                # Mark the state as visited\n                visited.add(next_state_hash)\n\n                # Check if the goal is satisfied in this new state\n                if next_state.satisfies(None, item):\n                    # Goal reached, return the path of actions that led to it\n                    return path + [action]\n                \n                # If the goal is not met, add the new state to the queue for further exploration\n                queue.append((next_state, path + [action]))\n\n    # If the queue becomes empty and the goal was never reached, it means the item is unreachable\n    return []", "island_id": 9, "scores": {"3": -1}}
